<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Signed into the macOS bundle (`bundle.macOS.entitlements` in tauri.conf.json). Releases are signed
  ad-hoc *with the hardened runtime* (`flags=0x10002(adhoc,runtime)`), and the hardened runtime turns
  each of these off unless the signature claims it. Nothing here matters to `tauri dev`, whose binary
  is unsigned and whose permissions belong to the terminal that launched it — which is why both
  failures below only ever showed up in the installed app.

  Never two hyphens in a row anywhere in this comment, not even to underline a heading: codesign's
  entitlements parser (AMFIUnserializeXML) follows the XML rule that forbids them inside a comment and
  fails the signature with "syntax error near line N", although `plutil -lint` passes the file. That
  broke the macOS release of 2026-10-09 at the signing step, after a full build.

  com.apple.security.device.audio-input
  «Dictar» and «Reuniones» read the microphone (cpal / AVCaptureDevice). Without this key macOS
  answers `requestAccessForMediaType:` with "denied" at once — no prompt, nothing written to TCC — so
  CodeFlow never appears under Privacidad › Micrófono and the user has no switch to turn on. Measured
  with a hardened ad-hoc test bundle: status 0 → request → NO in 0.00 s → status 2.
  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription (Info.plist) is the sentence; this is the permission to ask at all.

  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
  The whisper.cpp engine (dictation/engine.rs) and sherpa-onnx (meetings/speaker.rs) are downloaded
  on demand and loaded with `libloading`. Library validation only admits libraries signed by Apple or
  by the app's own Team ID, and an ad-hoc signature has no Team ID, so every such `dlopen` fails:
  "mapping process and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs". The files are verified by
  sha256 before they are unpacked; this key is what lets the process map them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
